WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.300
Contingency planning and supply chain also
close through governance, not technology.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.925
Contingency planning asks
for a plan, not a capability.

3
00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:12.498
You can have tested failover,
two circuits and good backups,

4
00:00:12.498 --> 00:00:17.383
and still carry an open finding, because
nothing says who declares a contingency,

5
00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:21.175
who gets told, what comes back first,
or when you're back to normal.

6
00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:24.513
And the mission owner, not
the database administrator,

7
00:00:24.513 --> 00:00:26.813
sets the maximum tolerable downtime.

8
00:00:26.813 --> 00:00:30.350
For a Moderate system, NIST
recommends a real exercise

9
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.337
with a restore from backup,
not just a tabletop.

10
00:00:33.337 --> 00:00:35.237
Supply chain shifted this year.

11
00:00:35.237 --> 00:00:38.706
The secure-development
attestation mandate was rescinded,

12
00:00:38.706 --> 00:00:42.037
and software bills of materials
became a contract choice.

13
00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:44.316
But the inventory is still required,

14
00:00:44.316 --> 00:00:48.038
and supply chain policy and
controls are in every baseline.

15
00:00:48.038 --> 00:00:50.742
Providers report their vulnerabilities;

16
00:00:50.742 --> 00:00:54.450
the agency reads those reports
into its own plan of action.

17
00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.540
Next, privacy and training.
